    22	                                              Through out this paper, K denotes an algebraically closed field of characteristic 0.
    23	                                              Let (f (x, y), g(x, y)) be a Jacobian pair. The Jacobian condition fx gy − fy gx = J is an expression
    24	                                           of two terms. We take a root of f (y)fy (y) in the Puiseux field K ≪ x−1 ≫ and plug in the
